// ============================================================================
// Projections · ENUM CONSTANTS  (pure column views — no joins, no closures)
//
// Named views over enum constants, for both the client (java_*) and any external
// library (lib_*). An enum *type* (enum Color { … }) is a type_decl with
// typeCategory = ENUM_TYPE (see types.dl); this file covers the *constants*
// (RED, GREEN) declared inside it.
//
// The constants matter because the parser tags an access like SomeEnum.CONSTANT as
// a FIELD reference with an empty referenced hash; the resolution layer falls back
// to this view (by constant name + owning enum) to type such a receiver. That
// fallback rule lives in resolution/, not here.
//
// Conventions: views only; one raw base relation per rule body; provenance tag first.
//
// java_enum_constant / lib_enum_constant cols (13):
//   0 name  1 qualifiedName  2 ordinal  3 arguments  4 argumentCount  5 hasBody
//   6 filePath  7 startLine  8 endLine  9 typeRegistryLinkHash (owner enum type)
//   10 ownerTypeName  11 ownerQualifiedName  12 enumConstantUniqueHash
// ============================================================================

// ── enum_decl(Prov, Name, QName, OwnerTypeHash, OwnerQName, EnumConstHash) ────
// An enum constant: its name, qualified name, and the enum type that owns it
// (both as a hash and as a qualified name — the resolver matches SomeEnum.CONSTANT
// by owning qualified name when only the qualifier's name is known).
enum_decl("client", name, qname, ownerType, ownerQName, h) :- java_enum_constant(name, qname, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, ownerType, _, ownerQName, h).
enum_decl("lib", name, qname, ownerType, ownerQName, h) :- lib_enum_constant(name, qname, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, ownerType, _, ownerQName, h).
